    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required emitting, in addition to the existing human-readable audit line, an immutable structured JSON event via the `AUDIT` logger on owner creation.\n\nI updated `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` to emit \u2014 after the existing audit line \u2014 a JSON object:\n\n```json\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nKey design points:\n\n- **`seq`** \u2014 a `static AtomicLong` incremented per create, so it's monotonically increasing across all creates (shared across OfficeFloor-instantiated instances).\n- **Structured, valid JSON** \u2014 serialized with the project's Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper`); a `LinkedHashMap` preserves the field order from the spec. Jackson 3's serialization exception is unchecked, so no `throws` clause is needed (which matters since OfficeFloor function signatures drive escalation handling).\n- **Forward-compatible identifier** \u2014 the requirement that the event carry \"the owner's current primary identifier... and whatever replaces it later\" is handled by a single `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` helper (returning `customerCode` today). When the identifier is unified into `memberId`, only that one method changes and the event follows.\n\nThe existing audit line is untouched, and the new event is emitted from the same `audit` step which runs after `SaveOwner` (so the owner id is assigned).\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` passes and the full `mvn test` suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).",
